    "biography": {
      "value": "<p>A male-presenting cyborg in a heavy chrome faceplate, with a single gold ring burning around the iris — the halo that gave him his name. He stands at the top of the loft stairs and does not sit down. Ever.</p><p>Unit-7 speaks maybe forty words a night. Thirty of them are “not tonight.”</p>",
      "director": "<p><strong>Plot hook:</strong> There is an old Ironclad serial still under that chrome, and somebody is quietly buying up scrap code that matches it. Halo does not know he is being reassembled on paper by a stranger. Whoever tells him first owns a very large favour.</p><p><strong>Running him:</strong> Neutral until the stairs are threatened, then immovable. He defends the loft, not the floor — Vexa handles the floor.</p>",
      "languages": []
    },
